    "Page 1422 states that the pore solutions of aged Portland cement pastes have often been observed to remain slightly oversaturated with respect to portlandite and ettringite, and that effective saturation indices divide the saturation index by the number of ions the solid dissociates into (2 for gypsum, 3 for portlandite, 15 for ettringite, 11 for monosulfate).",
